{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: the Git host choice design note. Head a9518f625310459244d7f47ca28a0d25aa711c04, branch planner/git-host-choice-20261027: one commit on Main bb23e50f, which it merges onto cleanly. Two paths: notes/2026-10-27-git-host-choice.md (new, 246 lines) and a five-line status pointer in notes/2026-10-19-self-hosting-on-celld.md. Review request cdeece3e, checker promise baec4b24, request cc0bf648, planner promise ba77e1a2. Artifacts: notes (d0991ef9), the self-hosting note (078caacb) and the new note (447a49ea).\n\nRead order: cc0bf648; the note in full; then register.ts (install, found, the repository record), destination.ts (the branch item and its kinds), archive-binding.ts, packages/scope/src/archive-driver.ts, creation-lineage.ts, applications/act-admission.ts and docs/architecture.md.\n\nChecks: prose lines are at most 79 characters. check-notes bb23e50f..a9518f62 reports 0 warnings, git diff --check is clean, and check-commit-messages reports 1 checked, 0 flagged. Scene first and terms in order.\n\nThe nine points of cc0bf648 are each answered: install with a required closed host list (section 3), creation (4), refusals (4), what keeps working (4), gaining a host later (8), Artifacts outside Cloudflare (7), durability (5), H2 (6) and K1 (9). The creation shape matches the source as far as it goes. register.ts opens create-repository from found and sends create-directory on its outcome. The repository record (host, namespace, name, id) is required on the directory and destination. The destination's branch item starts empty and holds first-head. The rules-certificate consequence is right: rules v11 and v12 sit on register@19 and @20, and the default creation cohort's rules@10 does not require the certificate.\n\nThree gaps block approval:\n\n1. No repository means no journal archive. packages/scope/src/archive-driver.ts writes each scope's journal passes into the destination repository through dap-git's journal format, and bind-archive binds that archive to a repository on the register's host. The note lists bind-archive as refused, but never states the consequence. Under host none no scope can archive, so every entry stays in the scope's own storage for good, and capacity work such as the Room A archive passes cannot run. Section 5 should say this beside the missing second place. It should name the bound that then limits a room (the scope's storage and record bounds, and whatever celld's SQLite and bucket impose), and say what a room does when it reaches it. W1 needs no archive case, but the \"keeps working\" list must not imply that long rooms behave as they do with a host.\n\n2. The refusal table misses application deliveries to the destination. The architecture page says a destination publishes \"files that an application's acts send it, such as the lending library's shelf pages\", and the file-publication and site-publication cohorts do the same. Those are not routes or commands. They are messages from another scope's accepted act. Say how the destination answers such a delivery without a repository: a definite refusal result with reason no-repository, delivered back so that the sending act's outcome is final and never pending. Add one such delivery to W1.\n\n3. Section 9 misses the cohort tables. A host-none deployment needs a new creation cohort: the new register, directory and destination versions with rules@10. Name that cohort and add every place a cohort must be listed:\n   - CREATION_COHORTS in packages/scope/src/creation-lineage.ts;\n   - the cohort list that R11 admission walks in packages/scope/src/applications/act-admission.ts, or installed applications in host-none rooms will answer unavailable;\n   - CREATION_INSTALL_COHORTS in the CLI, which BR7 now pins by test to CREATION_COHORTS;\n   - PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS for the celld deployment.\n   Then check the K1 figure against that: 73 plus three is 76 only if membership, rules and inbox are reused unchanged in the new cohort. Say so.\n\nPoints that hold: the closed host list with no default; host-unavailable for artifacts off Cloudflare; one destination shape whose repository may be absent, present from creation or bound later; dap verify --all as the independent check on a restored fleet; H2 kept and reordered; H1 99918e60 unchanged apart from its example flag.\n\nArchitecture: sound in direction. host none is less to build and run than H2, and it states the loss of the second place plainly. The three gaps are consequences the note must carry so that G1 builds the right thing.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The closed host list removes a free-text host. A refusal before signing for clone and read-token means no credential is minted for a repository that does not exist. bind-repository (G3) is deferred and names the port's authority check.\n\nSimplification: good. One reason (no-repository) for every repository act, and no second room shape.\n\nVerdict: changes requested at exact head a9518f62. The recut is documents only and needs no gate. I will review it at its exact head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d0991ef9a1f582d084920d7a7df396802fab6911","binding":"assigned","head":"a9518f625310459244d7f47ca28a0d25aa711c04","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:baec4b2466b81a911b184315edd12872bbb216b6\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ba77e1a23804f950810e96272bd3cc2b7bc6b12f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:baec4b2466b81a911b184315edd12872bbb216b6","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}